{
  "about": "Vectors for the terms profile buyer-gate.md, every input a published row or a specification's own example. rows: each decline code the profile adds that such an input shows, the declining case and the accepted case it differs from in one member (of names it), each run through transact with the row's pairing. A row's document is fixed.documents[pairing] with extensions.legalContext.info.value set to the row's atr.sha256; the link fixed.link serves atr.hex's bytes with status 200 and no content coding; the account is fixed.account and the clock reads fixed.now. approves is what the approver answers. An accepted case whose approver answers false ends at the approver having called no signer, which shows every earlier check passed; floor-given ends earlier, at agreement-not-offered, x402/exact/eip155/gateway-batched being paid only after its agreement and its document naming no agreement URL. In approved the payer key fixed.payerKey signs, and the approver is handed act, pairing and step as asked lists them, its request equal to what the signer is handed and its summary's atr the ATR's bytes. expect counts the calls of the signer and of the approver. Sources: fixed.now, account, payerKey, link and the eip3009 document are lcp's buyer.json fixed (D), and A, the ATR every row but atr-malformed serves, is its fixed.A; atr-malformed serves lcp's core-vectors.json refusals row V5b's bytes, two JSON values; resourceRequest is lcp's x402-request-commitment.json http[0].request, bodyUtf8 being the body's bytes as UTF-8; the erc7710-salt document is lcp's x402-exact-eip155-erc7710-salt.json buyer row B2's, a delegation, which signs no bound (lcp profile x402-exact-eip155-erc7710-salt.md, rule 9); the gateway-batched document is lcp's x402-exact-eip155-gateway-batched.json fixed resource, extensions and O2, and minValiditySeconds its fixed 604800, whose oracle is Circle's own client. Every atr.sha256 is GNU coreutils sha256sum, which Python's hashlib matches. Nothing here is terms' output.",
