  "parse": {
    "about": "The parse refuses exactly what lcp's assemble refuses in a party's bytes, its check 8 (core/content-not-json). lcp's core-vectors.json rows are the parse's rows too: refusals V5b (two JSON values) and V5c (bytes not UTF-8), refused, and jsonDepth's rows, accepted where accept is true. These rows are the cases that file does not hold, each a specification's own example: RFC 7493 section 2.2's integer and its range, read with Python's int, and its 1E400; RFC 8259 section 6's NaN and Infinity; RFC 8259 section 8.3's two spellings of one name; and RFC 8259 section 8.1's byte-order mark. hex is the text's bytes; accept says whether the parse takes it.",
